---
permalink: /search.json
# Not a page anyone should land on, and not one worth a line in the sitemap.
sitemap: false
---
{%- comment -%}
  The search index, built by Liquid at build time.

  This is the whole reason the site can have full-text search while still being
  built by GitHub Pages itself: it needs no plugin and no post-build step, only
  core filters. Anything that indexes the *rendered output* instead — Pagefind
  and friends — would mean owning the build, which this repo deliberately does
  not.

  Three kinds of thing go in, and each result says which it is:

    article  every post
    tag      the tag/*.md stubs, which carry a written title and description
             ("Food & Recipes") rather than the bare tag name off site.tags
    page     the standing pages and the teaching collection

  jsonify does the escaping, and it is the only escaping wanted here. An extra
  `escape` before it (as the tech1 original has) HTML-escapes the text as well,
  which puts a literal &amp; in the index and stops "R&D" ever matching itself.

  `content` on the articles is the bulk of this file by a wide margin — about
  140kB gzipped against a few kB for everything else — which is why
  assets/js/search.js does not fetch it until someone uses the search box.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign titled = site.pages | where_exp: "p", "p.title" -%}
[
{%- comment -%} ---- articles ------------------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- for post in site.posts -%}
{%- unless forloop.first -%},{%- endunless -%}
{
"type": "article",
{%- comment -%}
  Hidden posts stay IN the index. `hidden` keeps a post out of the listings, not
  out of the site — it is still built, still linkable, still in the feed. Search
  is how you reach one on purpose, so it is here, flagged, and the result is
  marked unlisted rather than quietly mixed in with the rest.
{%- endcomment -%}
"hidden": {{ post.hidden | default: false | jsonify }},
"title": {{ post.title | strip_html | jsonify }},
"subtitle": {{ post.subtitle | default: "" | strip_html | jsonify }},
"url": {{ post.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
"date": {{ post.date | date: site.minima.date_format | jsonify }},
"thumbnail": {{ post.thumbnail | default: "/assets/thumbs/default.png" | jsonify }},
"tags": {{ post.tags | jsonify }},
{%- comment -%}
  Block ends become full stops before the tags are stripped, so that two blocks
  running together do not weld their last and first words into one token —
  "…the endNext heading…" — which is both a word nobody will search for and a
  match nobody will get.
{%- endcomment -%}
"content": {{ post.content
  | replace: '</h', ' . </h'
  | replace: '</p', ' . </p'
  | replace: '</li', ' . </li'
  | replace: '</td', ' . </td'
  | replace: '<hr', ' . <hr'
  | strip_html
  | remove: '[['
  | remove: ']]'
  | normalize_whitespace
  | strip
  | jsonify }}
}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%} ---- tags ----------------------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- for stub in titled -%}
{%- if stub.layout == 'tagpage' -%},
{
"type": "tag",
"hidden": {{ stub.hidden | default: false | jsonify }},
"title": {{ stub.title | strip_html | jsonify }},
"subtitle": {{ stub.description | default: "" | strip_html | jsonify }},
"url": {{ stub.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
"date": "",
"thumbnail": "",
{%- comment -%}
  The bare tag as well as the written title, so that searching "food" reaches
  "Food & Recipes" and searching "uiux" reaches "UI/UX Projects".
{%- endcomment -%}
"tags": {{ stub.tag | split: ',' | jsonify }},
"content": {{ stub.description | default: "" | strip_html | jsonify }}
}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%} ---- pages ---------------------------------------------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- for p in titled -%}
{%- unless p.layout == 'tagpage' or p.layout == 'home' or p.layout == nil -%},
{
"type": "page",
"hidden": {{ p.hidden | default: false | jsonify }},
"title": {{ p.title | strip_html | jsonify }},
"subtitle": {{ p.subtitle | default: p.description | default: "" | strip_html | jsonify }},
"url": {{ p.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
"date": "",
"thumbnail": "",
"tags": [],
"content": {{ p.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | strip | jsonify }}
}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%} ---- the teaching collection, which is pages too --------- {%- endcomment -%}
{%- for course in site.teaching -%},
{
"type": "page",
"hidden": {{ course.hidden | default: false | jsonify }},
"title": {{ course.title | strip_html | jsonify }},
"subtitle": {{ course.subtitle | default: "" | strip_html | jsonify }},
"url": {{ course.url | relative_url | jsonify }},
"date": "",
"thumbnail": {{ course.thumbnail | default: "" | jsonify }},
"tags": [],
"content": {{ course.content | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | strip | jsonify }}
}
{%- endfor -%}
]
